*.egg-info/
*.db
data/uploads/
artifacts/real/
artifacts/*.csv
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CONSENTING-SME DATA — NEVER COMMIT.
# Real shop records collected under docs/REAL_DATA_PROTOCOL.md. Consent was
# given for university research, not for publication on GitHub. Even
# pseudonymised, a shop's full sales history is commercially sensitive and
# re-identifiable from its location and product mix.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/real_sme/

# Trained model artifacts (joblib) and benchmark outputs — regenerable.
artifacts/real/
artifacts/real_public/

# Online Retail II converted to CSV is ~94 MB — too large for git and fully
# reproducible (see docs/REAL_DATA_SOURCES.md's download+conversion steps).
# The small real datasets in this same folder (WFP prices, the Bangladeshi
# retailer demand series) ARE tracked — only this one file is excluded.
data/real_public/online_retail_II.csv

# Real-data candidate files we evaluated and set aside (~54 MB). Kept locally,
# never committed — see candidate_datasets_not_used/README.md for why neither
# qualifies as this thesis's real dataset.
candidate_datasets_not_used/

# One-off safety copy made by fix_annual_revenue.py before it rewrote the
# Annual_Revenue_BDT column in place. 11 MB, and the tracked dataset is the
# one everything derives from.
BD_Business_Analytics_Dataset_ORIGINAL_revenue_backup.csv

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated pipeline artifacts — all regenerable by run_all.py.
# Kept out of git so the repo stays reviewable as source, not data.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Stage 00 output: the star-schema tables + re-merged wide CSV (~12 MB)
normalized_data/

# Stage 01-05 intermediates: splits (11 MB), processed CSV (15 MB),
# fitted scaler/encoders, per-stage result objects
output/*.csv
output/*.pkl
output/*.txt

# Trained models — rf_model.pkl alone is 9 MB
output/models/

# The fake-forecast run kept only for local comparison. Never cite it,
# never commit it.
output/forecast_results_SIMULATED_backup.pkl

